{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tiff-cracked-pika","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Silent data loss in the store under concurrent write + in-flight review\n\n**Evidence is SECONDHAND** — reported by the session working [rebar:aec1-76e7-bb95-4c86], not\nreproduced by the filing session. Filed anyway because it is silent DATA LOSS in the ticket store,\nwhich is the system of record for every agent.\n\n### What was observed\n\n1. A `rebar edit --description` succeeded and was **verified by read-back at 14,997 chars**.\n2. A subsequent `rebar show` returned **10,582 chars** — an OLDER revision. Nothing reported an\n   error; no conflict, no `ConcurrencyError`, no exit 10.\n3. The agent's next read-modify-write then grafted new edits onto that stale text, **corrupting an\n   acceptance criterion** by splicing two unrelated fragments:\n\n       - [ ] a gate run persists `finish_reason` (recorded for triage, deliberately not rendered) (the windowed distinct-ratio that\n             rebar ticket 70bc establishes is computable from the record)\n\n4. Only a further read-back caught it. The agent rebuilt from a saved good revision and verified\n   the restore (15,666 chars, all markers present).\n\n### The reporter's hypothesis (unproven)\n\nThe ticket was being edited **while its own `rebar review-plan` was running**, and a review emits\nits own `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar events (`sidecar_emitted: true`). Store reconvergence between the\ntwo writers is the suspected cause. Corroborating signal: a later write to the same ticket with **no\nreview in flight** stayed intact.\n\n### Why this is worth a ticket rather than a note\n\n* **Optimistic concurrency did not fire.** The documented protection is a `ConcurrencyError`/exit 10\n  on a conflicting write. Here the write reported success, verified on read-back, and was then\n  silently rolled back — which is the one failure mode the concurrency design is supposed to make\n  impossible.\n* **Read-back verification is not sufficient**, which invalidates the standard mitigation every\n  agent is told to use. The read-back PASSED and the data was still lost afterwards.\n* The practical rule that emerged (\"never write to a ticket while its own review is running\") is an\n  undocumented landmine, and it conflicts with the normal remediate-then-review loop the plan-review\n  gate asks authors to perform.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the interaction is REPRODUCED deterministically (concurrent `rebar edit` + an in-flight\n      review emitting sidecar events on the same ticket), or the hypothesis is falsified and the\n      real trigger identified — the current evidence is a single secondhand observation\n- [ ] it is established why optimistic concurrency did not reject the losing write; a silent\n      last-writer-wins rollback on a ticket description is either a bug in the conflict detection\n      or an undocumented property of sidecar reconvergence\n- [ ] a write that will be discarded FAILS LOUDLY (`ConcurrencyError`/exit 10) rather than\n      reporting success and reverting afterwards\n- [ ] a regression test drives the concurrent-writer path and asserts the losing write is rejected,\n      not silently dropped\n- [ ] if the 'do not edit during a review' constraint is genuine and must stand, it is DOCUMENTED\n      where authors will hit it (the plan-review gate docs describe exactly the revise-then-review\n      loop that triggers it)\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q","id":"4136-a38d-7b33-4b9d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"A verified ticket description write was SILENTLY REVERTED to an older revision while that ticket's own plan-review was in flight"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785958439664433001,"uuid":"76db7efd-0267-46d5-aa8a-b1af9b318366"}